{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213421,"nonce":"Su2xqPiwrp+jj3jGR/D8VF1WoGY=","title":"Core scheduler over krio Task, with the reactor","message":"Ash's per-thread scheduler (std/src/fiber.rs: ready queue, timer heap,\n2 ms preemption epoch polled by compiled loops, M:N worker pool, park and\nblock_yield) moves into caribou and is redefined over krio-core::Task so that\nstackful fibers and compiled state machines (Zyntax async and effects,\nWrenLift's action loop and AOT transform) share one scheduler per world.\n\nThe reactor owns timers, sockets, file watches and channels; blocking\nprimitives park the fiber. Ash's sockets block the OS thread today and\nWrenLift's nested Fiber.yield spins; both are fixed here.\n\nPer-fiber host state (Ash's trap chain, Zyntax's effect handler stack) is\nkeyed by task id and swapped by the scheduler on every switch.\n\nFiber stacks register with the heap scanner; [saved_sp, stack_top) is the\nlive window, caller_sp covers the host stack while a fiber runs.","files":null}]}